[
    {
        "content": "<p>Could I ask for assistance rewriting a proof <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MvPowerSeries.instNoZeroDivisors#doc\">docs#MvPowerSeries.instNoZeroDivisors</a>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NoZeroDivisors</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">MvPowerSeries</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">eq_zero_or_eq_zero_of_mul_eq_zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ψ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">letI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinearOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinearOrder</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">swap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WellOrderingRel</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isWellOrder</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">linearOrder</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">letI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WellFoundedGT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">change</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsWellFounded</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WellOrderingRel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsWellOrder</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toIsWellFounded</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">simpa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lexOrder_eq_top_iff_eq_zero</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lexOrder_mul</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WithTop</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">add_eq_top</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I'm not exactly sure what is wrong (this is failing on an experimental branch where we are changing the behaviour of <code>inferInstanceAs</code>), but it's clearly ... not a pretty proof. (Why are the <code>letI</code> needed here in the first place? What API should we be using instead of <code>change</code>?)</p>\n<p>Would anyone be interested in rewriting this for me?</p>\n<p>(Extra bonus points if your new proof works both on <code>master</code> and on top of <code>49f4d609cf</code> on the <code>lean-pr-testing-12897</code> branch on <code>mathlib4-nightly-testing</code>, but just something sane on <code>master</code> would help me here.)</p>",
        "id": 580579553,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1773984913
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Perhaps <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"130609\">@Antoine Chambert-Loir</span>, as the author of this file?</p>",
        "id": 580579709,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1773985048
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(see also <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"287929\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/help.20in.20RingTheory.2EPolynomial.2EUniversalFactorizationRing/with/580579674\">#mathlib4 &gt; help in RingTheory.Polynomial.UniversalFactorizationRing</a>  for a related request)</p>",
        "id": 580579727,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1773985061
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NoZeroDivisors</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">MvPowerSeries</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">eq_zero_or_eq_zero_of_mul_eq_zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ψ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">letI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinearOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinearOrder</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">swap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WellOrderingRel</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isWellOrder</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">linearOrder</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">letI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WellFoundedGT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsWellOrder</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toIsWellFounded</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WellOrderingRel</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">simpa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lexOrder_eq_top_iff_eq_zero</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lexOrder_mul</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WithTop</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">add_eq_top</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>any better?</p>",
        "id": 580580020,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1773985312
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I guess it is better, at least avoiding the <code>change</code>. It doesn't solve my underlying problem (but that is probably still my fault, not this proof).</p>\n<p>On my branch I am getting</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mismatch</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">WellOrderingRel</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isWellOrder</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toIsWellFounded</span>\n<span class=\"n\">has</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">IsWellFounded</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WellOrderingRel</span>\n<span class=\"n\">but</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">WellFoundedGT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>it's possible this is because of a diamond I have unintentionally created earlier. :-(</p>",
        "id": 580580557,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1773985708
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Or maybe you're happier with</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/-- This instance is about `WellOrderingRel.isWellOrder.linearOrder`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WellFoundedLT</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wellOrderingRel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">letI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinearOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WellOrderingRel</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isWellOrder</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">linearOrder</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WellFoundedLT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">IsWellOrder</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toIsWellFounded</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WellOrderingRel</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- This instance is about `LinearOrder.swap`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WellFoundedGT</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">swap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinearOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">WellFoundedLT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">letI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinearOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">swap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WellFoundedGT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">‹</span><span class=\"n\">WellFoundedLT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"bp\">›</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NoZeroDivisors</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">MvPowerSeries</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">eq_zero_or_eq_zero_of_mul_eq_zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ψ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">letI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinearOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinearOrder</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">swap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WellOrderingRel</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isWellOrder</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">linearOrder</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">simpa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lexOrder_eq_top_iff_eq_zero</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lexOrder_mul</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WithTop</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">add_eq_top</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 580580605,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1773985755
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(though I would worry that those instances might misbehave)</p>",
        "id": 580580994,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1773986097
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks! That helped me localize the problem: my changes have broken the reducibility of <code>LinearOrder.swap</code>.</p>",
        "id": 580581390,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1773986414
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I suspect my intuition for those instances being risky is based on heuristics that may no longer apply, so they might still be a good idea</p>",
        "id": 580582115,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1773986784
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't think I'll do it, but if anyone would like to find a reasonable home for those two instances and PR them, I think they would be useful.</p>",
        "id": 580582203,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1773986832
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"310045\">@Eric Wieser</span> , do you want me to do it?</p>",
        "id": 580586193,
        "sender_full_name": "Antoine Chambert-Loir",
        "timestamp": 1773989413
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Go for it!</p>",
        "id": 580586392,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1773989544
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/36892\">#36892</a></p>",
        "id": 580596085,
        "sender_full_name": "Antoine Chambert-Loir",
        "timestamp": 1773994224
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is that really a reasonable instance?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/-- This instance is about `LinearOrder.swap`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WellFoundedGT</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">swap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinearOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">WellFoundedLT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">letI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinearOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">swap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WellFoundedGT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">‹</span><span class=\"n\">WellFoundedLT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"bp\">›</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I would understand giving this as an instance on the order dual. But on sigma itself, it feels weird.</p>",
        "id": 580596784,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1773994484
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I was worried myself, but it seems to work. The context is that in several applications (this is due to the way the lexicographic ordering is set up, but I presume that defining it the other way round would break other parts), one needs a <code>WellFoundedGT</code> ordering on a given type, and one doesn't have the luxury of setting it up as an order dual.</p>",
        "id": 580597597,
        "sender_full_name": "Antoine Chambert-Loir",
        "timestamp": 1773994793
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But what is the linear order on the given type, then? Does it have simultaneously two linear order instances, <code>l</code> and <code>l.swap</code>?</p>",
        "id": 580598900,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1773995241
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>AFAI, it has indeed two, but the first one has <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=WellFoundedLT#doc\">docs#WellFoundedLT</a>, the second one (its <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=LinearOrder.swap#doc\">docs#LinearOrder.swap</a>) has <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=WellFoundedGT#doc\">docs#WellFoundedGT</a>. And fortunately, one does not play with the caseswhere <code>σ</code> is finite and prove that the initial one already had <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=WellFoundedGT#doc\">docs#WellFoundedGT</a>.</p>",
        "id": 580599288,
        "sender_full_name": "Antoine Chambert-Loir",
        "timestamp": 1773995386
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If there are two different orders around simultaneously, this sounds like a recipe for disaster :-)</p>",
        "id": 580599815,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1773995550
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But maybe I'm wrong and it only within the proof that it has two orders, but the typeclass inference system detects the correct one for that proof.</p>",
        "id": 580600834,
        "sender_full_name": "Antoine Chambert-Loir",
        "timestamp": 1773995992
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, normally it's only the one that has been declared latest which will be used. So one can definitely do this kind of things if one knows what one is doing -- but it's tricky, and often not very robust.</p>",
        "id": 580603989,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1773997130
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I have updated <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/36892\">#36892</a>:  </p>\n<ul>\n<li>removed the illegitimate instance but kept the other one, </li>\n<li>deprecated <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=LinearOrder.swap#doc\">docs#LinearOrder.swap</a>, </li>\n<li>added <code>exists_wellFoundedGT</code> that shows the existence of a linear order which satisfies <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=WellFoundedGT#doc\">docs#WellFoundedGT</a>, </li>\n<li>and used it to refactor the proof of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MvPowerSeries.instNoZeroDivisors#doc\">docs#MvPowerSeries.instNoZeroDivisors</a>.</li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 584540506,
        "sender_full_name": "Antoine Chambert-Loir",
        "timestamp": 1775768566
    }
]